\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The breakaway problem. (a) A rod held off its centre of mass pivots under gravity; at the first slip friction drops from static to kinetic and the rod can run past the limit $\varphi _{\lim }$. (b) Energy balance from rest at $\varphi _0=0$: the rod stops where friction work (lines of slope $k=F/(rF_h)$) catches up with gravity work. With the same grip, $r=1.5$ stops far later than $r=1$. The shield requires the friction line to lie above the chord to $\varphi _{\lim }$. (c) The emulated friction law: static capacity until the relative speed exceeds $\omega _{\rm  slip}$, kinetic capacity $\mu _t/r$ until it falls below $\omega _{\rm  stick}$.}}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mech}{{2}{2}{The breakaway problem. (a) A rod held off its centre of mass pivots under gravity; at the first slip friction drops from static to kinetic and the rod can run past the limit $\varphi _{\lim }$. (b) Energy balance from rest at $\varphi _0=0$: the rod stops where friction work (lines of slope $k=F/(rF_h)$) catches up with gravity work. With the same grip, $r=1.5$ stops far later than $r=1$. The shield requires the friction line to lie above the chord to $\varphi _{\lim }$. (c) The emulated friction law: static capacity until the relative speed exceeds $\omega _{\rm slip}$, kinetic capacity $\mu _t/r$ until it falls below $\omega _{\rm stick}$}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Shielded residual control. A probe returns the measured state and the last grip at which the object was stuck. The model controller proposes an action and the residual policy corrects it. The shield passes certified actions (clipping grip up, or the hold down, to the bound) and falls back to the model step (defer) or stops (decline) when no certified action exists.}}{2}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method}{{3}{2}{Shielded residual control. A probe returns the measured state and the last grip at which the object was stuck. The model controller proposes an action and the residual policy corrects it. The shield passes certified actions (clipping grip up, or the hold down, to the bound) and falls back to the model step (defer) or stops (decline) when no certified action exists}{figure.caption.3}{}}
