\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Where a certified pivot from rest exists. Shaded blue: the shield's grip floor as a fraction of $F_{\rm  last}$ (smaller means larger steps). Pink: no certified release. The shield's limit (dashed) lies on the physical limit $r^\ast $ (orange). For $r=1.1$, targets shallower than about 0.75\,rad are infeasible.}}{3}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:feas}{{4}{3}{Where a certified pivot from rest exists. Shaded blue: the shield's grip floor as a fraction of $F_{\rm last}$ (smaller means larger steps). Pink: no certified release. The shield's limit (dashed) lies on the physical limit $r^\ast $ (orange). For $r=1.1$, targets shallower than about 0.75\,rad are infeasible}{figure.caption.4}{}}
